WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.423
[MUSIC]

00:00:04.423 --> 00:00:08.890
My sister Fernando and
I grew up loving animals.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:14.313
Our best family vacation was
a trip to Disney's Animal Kingdom.

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:18.706
I was five years old and
I went on the safari ride.

00:00:18.706 --> 00:00:24.112
When I saw the reenactment of poachers
trying to steal a baby elephant,

00:00:24.112 --> 00:00:28.722
my heart beat so hard,
I still remember how hard it bounded.

00:00:28.722 --> 00:00:32.476
When the elephant was rescued,
this was Disney after all.

00:00:32.476 --> 00:00:35.203
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I cried with relief.

00:00:35.203 --> 00:00:41.633
Little did I know that one day Fernando
and I would have our own rescue mission.

00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:46.958
Six years ago, we met a tiger.

00:00:46.958 --> 00:00:51.603
He was living in this small town in Mexico
in a public park where the government

00:00:51.603 --> 00:00:54.325
couldn't afford to pay for his medication.

00:00:54.325 --> 00:01:01.069
His home was a windowless concrete hut,
full of old, filthy hay.

00:01:01.069 --> 00:01:05.647
The tiger's name was Rajah,
which means Indian king.

00:01:05.647 --> 00:01:10.597
But Rajah wasn't the sort of
majestic creature you'd expect

00:01:10.597 --> 00:01:12.604
to see in a Disney movie.

00:01:12.604 --> 00:01:16.493
He was so weak, he couldn't even stand up.

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:20.887
He had red raw open source on his legs.

00:01:20.887 --> 00:01:26.787
When I looked at Rajah and I really
look into his deep dive watery eyes,

00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:28.895
I could feel his misery.

00:01:28.895 --> 00:01:33.640
And all I wanted to do was to take
him out of that concrete prison and

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.967
find a place where he could go and
be healthy and safe again.

00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:43.741
Trying to find such a place, Fernando and
I contacted a number of sanctuaries.

00:01:43.741 --> 00:01:48.381
Finally, one in Colorado
agreed to take Rajah.

00:01:48.381 --> 00:01:54.554
After countless meetings and phone calls
and paperwork over an eight week period,

00:01:54.554 --> 00:02:00.217
we finally convince the Mexican
government to let go of Rajah.

00:02:00.217 --> 00:02:07.850
But before we could do the transport,
Rajah died.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:13.247
When Fernando and I heard the news,
we held each other and

00:02:13.247 --> 00:02:18.083
we decided that we do
everything we could to prevent

00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:24.167
other animals from sharing
Rajah's unhappy ending.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:27.695
In 2015, we had our first test.

00:02:27.695 --> 00:02:32.635
Mexico's Congress passed a well
intentional law that bans animal

00:02:32.635 --> 00:02:34.934
performances from services.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:41.401
From one day to another 1200
animals needed a new place to live.

00:02:41.401 --> 00:02:46.207
The lack of suitable places
to relocate these animals

00:02:46.207 --> 00:02:50.274
resulted in the death of 1,000 of them.

00:02:50.274 --> 00:02:53.614
Fernando and
I started a social media campaign.

00:02:53.614 --> 00:02:59.095
We contacted international sanctuaries and
we talked to the Mexican authorities.

00:02:59.095 --> 00:03:03.950
And then we learned that this was
just the tip of the ice berg.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:08.977
In the part 15 years in Mexico alone,
45,000 wild

00:03:08.977 --> 00:03:15.252
animals have been victims of abuse,
exploitation and wild life trade.

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:23.733
And the ones that were lucky enough to be
rescued, didn't have a safe place to go.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:31.316
Sadly, this is a problem
that goes far beyond Mexico.

00:03:31.316 --> 00:03:36.665
According to the World's Wildlife
Organization, environmental degradation

00:03:36.665 --> 00:03:41.697
together with illegal wildlife trade
has lead to an extinction rate between

00:03:41.697 --> 00:03:46.826
a 1000 and 10,000 times higher
than the natural extinction rate.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:51.722
Since 1976, we;'ve wiped out 60,

00:03:51.722 --> 00:03:55.172
60% of the world wildlife.

00:03:55.172 --> 00:04:00.140
Recently, the last male white rhino died.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.270
There are still two female
white rhinos in the planet.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.930
But when they die,
the whole species will be gone forever.

00:04:12.016 --> 00:04:17.734
The heart of the problem lies in the lack
of awareness about wildlife conservation.

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:23.488
In some cultures, rhino horn is
used as it was a miracle cure.

00:04:23.488 --> 00:04:27.667
In others, ivory is a symbol of status.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:32.572
But it's not just exotic
products that harm wild life.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:36.534
If you use shampoo or eat ice cream,

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:42.620
these everyday products
typically contain palm oil.

00:04:44.594 --> 00:04:49.110
Every hour,
rain forest area equivalent to 300

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:53.521
soccer fields are being
lost to palm oil farming,

00:04:53.521 --> 00:04:59.630
leaving hundreds of wild animals and
endangered species homeless.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:08.986
Thankfully, most of the time when
people learn about the negative

00:05:08.986 --> 00:05:13.691
consequences their behaviors have,
they start caring.

00:05:13.691 --> 00:05:18.688
Each one of us in this room can make
a difference by changing some of our

00:05:18.688 --> 00:05:19.644
behaviors.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:27.426
In 2017, Fernando and
I decided to built Latin America's

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:34.123
first wildlife sanctuary to house and
rehabilitate abused wild animals.

00:05:34.123 --> 00:05:38.619
Located in 50 acres in
the center of Mexico,

00:05:38.619 --> 00:05:44.846
San Tuay is being designed to
accommodate 200 wild animals,

00:05:44.846 --> 00:05:49.131
including bears, elephants and big cats.

00:05:49.131 --> 00:05:54.283
Through the best veterinary practices and
top notch facilities,

00:05:54.283 --> 00:06:00.450
our sanctuary will provide these animals
with a healthy and safe place to live.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:05.205
In San Tuay, visitors will be able to
witness the consequences of illegal

00:06:05.205 --> 00:06:08.433
wildlife trade and
environmental degradation.

00:06:08.433 --> 00:06:14.534
But they will also learn ways in which
they can contribute to the solution.

00:06:14.534 --> 00:06:19.580
Our end goal is to replicate this
kind of sanctuaries across the world.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:24.572
Currently, we're in the process
of raising funds, and hopefully,

00:06:24.572 --> 00:06:28.884
in a few months, we will be able
to start building a place that

00:06:28.884 --> 00:06:32.535
will change the lives of
hundreds of wild animals.

00:06:32.535 --> 00:06:39.366
But most importantly, the behaviors and
minds of thousands of visitors.

00:06:42.182 --> 00:06:47.900
However, you don't have to build
a wildlife sanctuary to make a difference.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:52.976
Minor changes in your
everyday habits could

00:06:52.976 --> 00:06:58.059
save the lives of
hundreds of wild animals.

00:06:58.059 --> 00:07:04.727
A few people have asked me, why should
I care about saving wild animals?

00:07:04.727 --> 00:07:07.910
Well, let me tell you.

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:14.412
Biodiversity is fundamental for
a healthy ecosystem.

00:07:14.412 --> 00:07:21.498
A healthy ecosystem is fundamental for
a healthy and sustainable economy.

00:07:21.498 --> 00:07:26.968
These animals are a fundamental
part of that biodiversity.

00:07:26.968 --> 00:07:32.170
But mostly I just want to show
them a picture of Rajah, to me,

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:37.586
the reason why we need to save
these animals is self-evident.

00:07:39.415 --> 00:07:45.069
There are many things you can
do to help protect wild animals.

00:07:45.069 --> 00:07:49.792
But today,
I want you to leave with three in mind.

00:07:49.792 --> 00:07:52.991
First, reduce food waste,

00:07:52.991 --> 00:07:58.469
40% of the food grown on
the planet is wasted.

00:07:58.469 --> 00:08:05.791
Growing that food destroys habitats, so
let's not grow so much more than we need.

00:08:05.791 --> 00:08:10.955
Second, buy environmentally
responsible products.

00:08:10.955 --> 00:08:15.579
Look at the ingredients,
make sure they are responsibly

00:08:15.579 --> 00:08:19.253
sourced especially if
it contains palm oil.

00:08:19.253 --> 00:08:23.487
Third, reduce meat consumption,

00:08:23.487 --> 00:08:27.727
try to shift from red to white meat.

00:08:27.727 --> 00:08:31.354
The livestock industry is responsible for

00:08:31.354 --> 00:08:36.500
a disproportionate amount of
annual habitat destruction.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:41.707
And then you can always volunteer or
donate to sanctuaries like mine.

00:08:43.642 --> 00:08:51.346
[LAUGH] Today I feel very lucky to
be a part of the GSB community.

00:08:51.346 --> 00:08:57.326
People like you have the power
to inspire thousands of others.

00:08:57.326 --> 00:09:03.402
Through the companies you will create,
through the policies you will influence,

00:09:03.402 --> 00:09:06.459
and through the children you will raise.

00:09:06.459 --> 00:09:13.869
Let's all work together in creating real
life happy endings for animals like Rajah.

00:09:13.869 --> 00:09:14.595
Thank you.

00:09:14.595 --> 00:09:19.775
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:09:19.775 --> 00:09:22.238
[MUSIC]

